{
  "description": "Shared notification envelope v1 test vectors (ADR 0008). Single source of truth for the encrypted Agent Notification payload, consumed by both the Node plugin tests (encrypt direction) and the Swift app tests (decrypt direction). Envelopes were generated with raw AES-256-GCM calls, independent of both implementations, and resealed the same way when `paneId` values were updated to observed-family herdr identifiers (opaque alphanumeric `w…:p…` strings, uppercase included — not tmux-style `%N`). `key` is the 32-byte Notification Key and `keyId` its derived id, both unpadded base64url. `envelope` is the exact canonical envelope string; non-`decodeOnly` valid vectors must be reproduced byte-for-byte by the encrypt side. `decodeOnly: true` marks envelopes that must decrypt to `payload` but are not a canonical encoding of it. `project` and `title` are the optional display fields, omitted from the plaintext when absent; `attention` is the optional per-Host badge count (Blocked + Done agents), omitted when absent but sent when 0. `reply` is a Chat Mode Agent's final reply, given raw in `payload`; the encrypt side normalizes it (CRLF to LF, C0 controls other than tab and newline stripped, lone surrogates replaced with U+FFFD, trimmed, capped at 1000 bytes of JSON-escaped UTF-8 on a grapheme boundary with `…`; when the sealed `ct` would exceed 2,800 bytes it is re-capped at 500 bytes, and then dropped), and `expectedReply` is the normalized value the plaintext carries. `expectedBody`, when present, is the alert body the app must render. Invalid vectors must fail decryption with the given typed error.",
